diff --git a/content/getting-started/lists.md b/content/getting-started/lists.md
index dde2111..30ac5ab 100644
--- a/content/getting-started/lists.md
+++ b/content/getting-started/lists.md
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@ Many values can be changed right where they are shown, without opening an edit f
 - a project's manager and a recurring ticket's technician
 - an asset's status, location and assigned contact, and a contact's location
 
+**Cancel**, at the top of the list, closes it without changing anything - as <kbd>Esc</kbd> does, or a click anywhere else.
+
 ![Clicking a ticket's priority in the tickets list opens a picker with Low, Medium, High and Urgent](gs-quick-pick.webp "Click a value to change it in place")
 
 ## Copy buttons
@@ -81,4 +83,6 @@ Most records also have a full page of their own. They share one layout:
 
 Forms have an icon in front of every field. Long forms are split into tabs; if you save with a required field empty on another tab, ITFlow takes you to it.
 
+A field with a list of choices opens it under the field, with a search box when the list is long. **Cancel** at the top closes it without changing the field, and **Done** closes one where you tick several. A click anywhere else closes it too, a reply or other text box included.
+
 ITFlow asks before it deletes or turns off anything, and before you leave a page with a reply or note you haven't saved.
diff --git a/content/service-desk/canned-responses.md b/content/service-desk/canned-responses.md
index 0bb8228..cfc0687 100644
--- a/content/service-desk/canned-responses.md
+++ b/content/service-desk/canned-responses.md
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ A canned response is a reply you write once and reuse: "we've received your tick
 2. Click **Canned response**, or type <kbd>/</kbd> in the reply and keep typing to narrow the list.
 3. Search by name or by what it says, and click one (or press <kbd>Enter</kbd> for the first).
 
+Changed your mind? **Cancel**, beside the search, closes the list and puts you back in your reply - or just click into the reply.
+
 ![The canned response picker over the reply box](sd-canned-picker.webp "The picker: the responses for this ticket's category first, then the ones for every ticket, each with what it sets up")
 
 The response goes in where your cursor is. The ones offered are those for the ticket's category and those for every ticket; your own come first, as **Yours**.
